WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.879
Good morning John, here in the
US the moment has arrived.

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:05.100
Everyone over the age of 16
can get the COVID vaccine.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.250
Over 200 million doses have been
administered, and around 40%

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.720
of people have gotten at
least one dose.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:11.830
And yet.

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.099
The graph of people
getting vaccinated everyday,

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:17.500
it’s starting to stop do this,
where it’s going higher every day,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.529
it’s starting to go less and less
everyday.

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:20.529
And the reason for

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:22.750
this is largely younger people,
by which I mean people under

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.380
the age of 50 not getting their
vaccine immediately.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.380
It could be

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.660
that you, watching this video
right now are one of those people,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.680
or maybe you know one of those
people and you want to send them

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.680
this video.

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.410
So I’m going to go,
very quickly, through a few of the

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.940
reasons why I’ve heard young
people specifically say they haven’t

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.060
gotten vaccinated yet.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.550
And first, I think tremendously under

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.410
examined, is just that like, it’s a slightly
unpleasant task that I

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.890
don’t want to add to my list of
things to do.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:44.890
And since now you

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.840
can do it at any time, people
are putting it off.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.910
Schedules are busy, and you know
that the day after your second

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.200
dose you might feel pretty crummy,
I certainly did.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.200
So why not put it off

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.200
to a more convenient time?

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.090
But as with all procrastinations, look

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.690
there’s not really a better time than now.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.690
But you also have to look

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.000
at what the trade off is, like we’re
dealing with mild inconvenience

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.300
that is scheduled versus unscheduled
major inconvenience and maybe worse.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.710
The symptoms of COVID suck
no matter how old you are.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.311
COVID does kill young people, it just
doesn’t kill very many of them.

00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:15.060
The hospitalization rates are pretty high,
and spending a bunch of time

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.860
at the hospital is so bad.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.350
It’s also like a burden on

00:01:18.350 --> 00:01:21.870
healthcare workers who are
overburdened enough right now.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.130
There are also a bunch of long
term side effects from getting COVID

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.350
that we don’t understand super well
right now, and those sometimes

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.860
also happen when people
get very mild cases.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.930
But even if you get none of that,
it’s still really inconvenient to get

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.020
COVID. You feel like crap, you
have to quarantine.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:37.020
It’s inconvenient

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.990
for you and everyone else
in your world.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.810
So why not decrease the odds 
of that happening by 95%?

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:42.810
But maybe you’re not worried

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:43.810
about yourself at all.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.610
It’s still really
important to recognize that every

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:49.070
person except like the first
person who gets COVID, gets it

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.070
from somebody else.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.520
And it’s very
easy to not know when you are the

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.240
person who got someone sick
because a lot of people get sick

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.120
by being exposed to people who
are infected but don’t even

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.120
know that they are.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.840
If you’re
vaccinated, the odds of you

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.960
getting another person sick
go way, way, way down.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.280
And then much more unlikely,
but even scarier.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.280
Every one of the new

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.890
COVID variants that we’re talking
about right now, every one of them

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.740
evolved inside of a person.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:20.150
And we will never know who that person was.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:24.069
But I think we all can agree that
we don’t want to be that person.

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.410
Nobody wants to be the breeding ground
from which a new variant of COVID

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.410
emerges.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.090
You can prevent yourself
from being that person by

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:31.090
getting a vaccine.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.090
Now finally I’ve also heard some

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.590
people saying that, you know,
I got COVID, or I think I got COVID,

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.501
or I might as well just get COVID
and I can get immunity that way.

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.556
Leaving aside the fact that it is a big deal

00:02:40.556 --> 00:02:43.776
 and you might infect someone 
for who it is an even bigger deal,

00:02:43.776 --> 00:02:47.159
immunity from getting COVID is 
much less effective at preventing

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:49.850
future COVID infections than the vaccines are.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.000
So if you’ve
had COVID or you think you

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.760
might have, or if you think, I’ll just
get it and get immune that way,

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.770
none of that works.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.770
You need a vaccine.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.571
I understand that every person is
experiencing this differently, and

00:02:59.571 --> 00:03:00.950
also that it’s frustrating.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:01.950
And annoying.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.000
Like this things has been in

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.459
charge of our lives for too long.

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:07.041
And for many people, a vaccine

00:03:07.041 --> 00:03:09.420
feels like a way of taking back
control.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.070
And for others, it feels

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.959
like more control that they’re
giving up.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.270
For me, it felt like

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:15.440
taking back control.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.680
And I think to some extent,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.840
because the vaccines are a
really big deal, and they are

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.790
such a triumph of hard work
and human ingenuity, that it’s

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.660
easy to think, like, I have to
think really hard about this.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.770
It’s something to worry about,
and to fret over.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:29.770
But my friends,

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:30.770
it’s really not.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:34.030
The decision here
is simple, it is both a big deal but

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.629
also not a big deal.

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:37.569
It’s just not a
big deal.

00:03:37.569 --> 00:03:38.569
So if you need one final

00:03:38.569 --> 00:03:41.600
reason to go get a vaccine,
hi I’m Hank Green.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.600
I make science videos.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:44.950
I’ve been making
educational videos for people for

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.600
free on the internet for over 10 years,
and maybe you want to do

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.600
me a favor!

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.770
It’s super easy,
there’s a link in the description

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.150
you can click on it, put in your
zip code, and make your appointment

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:53.620
for getting your COVID vaccine.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.620
Put it in your phone,

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.620
then go do it.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.620
And get a free donut.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.659
John, I’ll see you
on Tuesday.

